window.AG_CHAPTERS["06"] = {"id":"06","title":"The Cloth Merchant&#39;s Year","titleZh":"錢掌櫃的一年","patient":{"name":"Qian Bo 錢掌櫃","sprite":"man"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-town.jpg","key":"rain"},"pattern":"Liver Yang Rising 肝陽上亢","principle":"anchor the rising yang above, and nourish the yin that failed to hold it below","tongue":"red body, thin yellow coating","pulseNote":{"en":"Long, taut and forceful under the finger — it pushes back, and it does not soften at the deeper level.","zh":"端直以長，按之有力，沉取亦不減其勁"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>Fēngchí GB20</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"GB20","zh":"風池","py":"Fēngchí","x":278,"y":578,"img":"art/body-head-lateral.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"decoys":[{"x":100,"y":440},{"x":232,"y":392},{"x":247,"y":522},{"x":300,"y":660},{"x":214,"y":300}],"note":"<b>風池 Fēngchí GB20</b> — below the occiput, in the depression between the sternocleidomastoid and the trapezius, level with GV16.<br>枕骨下，胸鎖乳突肌與斜方肌之間凹陷處，平風府。"},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"Everything he complains of is <b>above</b>. Ask deliberately about what is <b>below</b> — that is where this pattern hides its other half.","zh":"其所苦皆在上。當刻意問其下——此證之另一半藏在下部。"},"look":{"en":"A red body says heat. What you must decide is whether the coating is full and yellow, or scant — that is heat with substance versus heat from emptiness.","zh":"舌紅主熱。當辨其苔黃厚或少：一為有形之熱，一為虛熱。"},"pulse":{"en":"Wiry is the Liver. Press deeper: does it hold its force, or thin out underneath?","zh":"弦者肝脈。當沉取：其力仍在，抑或按之轉細？"},"dx":{"en":"Three steps: locate the <b>organ</b> → decide <b>above and below</b> → then decide what you treat <b>first</b>.","zh":"三步：定其臟 → 辨其上下 → 定標本先後。"},"rx":{"en":"Yang has risen because something below stopped holding it down. Treat both ends, or it comes straight back up.","zh":"陽亢者，下無所涵也。上下並取，否則旋治旋發。"},"tech":{"en":"This point sits below the occiput. Angle and depth are not a matter of style here.","zh":"此穴在枕骨之下。針之方向與深度，非關手法喜好。"}},"reactions":[{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen says nothing. He is watching the merchant's colour.","zh":"參師父不作聲，只看著掌櫃的面色。"},{"who":"patient","en":"Qian Bo presses two fingers hard against his temple without noticing he is doing it.","zh":"錢掌櫃用兩指使勁按著太陽穴，自己並沒有察覺。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy sets down the tea very quietly, and steps back.","zh":"藥童把茶輕輕放下，退開一步。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"You remember Liu Sanniang, in the teahouse. Constraint. This is the same road, further along.\"","zh":"「你還記得茶館的柳三娘，那是鬱。這是同一條路，走遠了些。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"It's the accounts,\" he says. \"And the wine. I know. My wife says the same.\"","zh":"「是帳，」他說，「還有酒。我知道，我內人也這麼說。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Constraint becomes heat, heat becomes fire, fire becomes rising yang. Find out how far it has gone.\"","zh":"「鬱久化熱，熱極化火，火盛則陽亢。你要問出它走到哪一步。」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"excess_def","look":"cold_heat","pulse":"cold_heat","dx":"excess_def","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"channel_organ"},"reward":{"cardEn":"Anchor Above, Nourish Below","cardZh":"上潛下滋","cardTxt":"When yang rises it is rarely because yang is too strong — it is because the yin below stopped anchoring it. Subdue the branch above and nourish the root below, or it rises again the moment you stop.","herbId":"baishao","herbEn":"White Peony Root","herbZh":"白芍","herbImg":"art/card-baishao.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Sour, bitter and slightly cold. It nourishes blood and softens the Liver — sour and inward-moving, the counterweight to anything that rises and scatters."},"endings":{"three":["Two months later Qian Bo says the headaches come perhaps once a fortnight, and pass. \"My knees are still my knees,\" he adds, \"but I can get up the stairs.\"<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You treated the top and the bottom. Anyone can quiet a headache for a week. You asked why it kept coming back.\"","兩個月後，錢掌櫃說頭痛約半月一發，且發而能止。「膝蓋還是那樣，」他又說，「不過上樓上得動了。」<br><b>參師父：</b>「你上下俱治。壓一週的頭痛誰都會，你問的是它為何再來。」"],"two":["The headaches ease, then return after a bad week at the counter.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You settled what was rising. You did not ask what had stopped holding it down.\"","頭痛好轉，鋪子忙了一週又發。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你潛了上亢之陽，卻沒問是誰不再涵住它。」"],"one":["No change, and he is short with the herb boy on the way out.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Go back to the second question. Everything he told you was about his head. What did you not ask about?\"","沒有起色，出門時還對藥童發了脾氣。<br><b>參師父：</b>「回到第二問。他說的全是頭上的事——你沒問的是什麼？」"],"titles":["Qian Bo Climbs the Stairs","Qian Bo Has a Quieter Fortnight","Qian Bo Will Need Another Visit"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"Five patients now. Four of them were one thing: empty, or full. This one is both at once.","cn":"五個病人了。前四個是一件事：不是虛，就是實。這一個，兩者同時。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Doctor. Qian, I keep the cloth shop on the east street. My head has been splitting for the best part of a year.","cn":"大夫。姓錢，東街布莊的。這頭痛，斷斷續續快一年了。"},{"w":"patient","en":"It comes with dizziness, and my ears ring. Worse when I lose my temper, worse after wine. My face goes hot.","cn":"痛起來頭暈，耳朵嗡嗡響。一發火就重，喝了酒也重，臉會發燙。"},{"w":"master","en":"Heat rising to the head. That much is plain from across the room. But plain is not the same as complete.","cn":"熱上衝頭，隔著屋子就看得出。然而顯而易見，不等於完整。"},{"w":"master","en":"Ask him about his head. Then — and this is the part students forget — ask him about his knees.","cn":"問他的頭。然後——這一步學生最常漏——問他的膝蓋。"}],"qa":[{"q":"Tell me about the headache and dizziness. Where, and when?","cq":"頭痛與眩暈：痛在何處？何時發作？","good":1,"a":"Both sides, up here by my temples. The room tilts if I stand too fast. Always worse when I'm angry.","ca":"兩邊太陽穴這裡。起得急就天旋地轉。一動氣必定重。","clue":{"en":"Temporal headache and dizziness, worse with anger","zh":"顳部頭痛、眩暈，遇怒則甚"},"note":"The sides of the head are Shaoyang, and anger is the Liver's own emotion. Together they place the disorder before you have touched the pulse. 頭側屬少陽，怒為肝志。二者合觀，未切脈而病位已定。"},{"q":"Do your ears ring? Loud and sudden, or faint and worse when you are tired?","cq":"耳鳴嗎？是驟起聲大，還是聲細遇勞則甚？","good":1,"a":"Loud. Like cicadas. It roars when the headache is bad.","ca":"聲大，像蟬。頭痛重的時候更響。","clue":{"en":"Loud tinnitus, worse with the headache","zh":"耳鳴聲大，隨頭痛而甚"},"note":"Loud, sudden tinnitus rising with anger is excess in the Liver and Gallbladder. Faint ringing that worsens with fatigue would be Kidney deficiency alone. 耳鳴聲大、驟起、遇怒而甚，屬肝膽實。聲細遇勞則甚者，單屬腎虛。"},{"q":"How is your lower back, and your knees?","cq":"腰如何？膝蓋如何？","good":1,"a":"Aching, both of them. The knees give way on the stairs. I thought that was just my age.","ca":"腰痠，膝也軟。上樓腿發虛。我只當是上了年紀。","clue":{"en":"Aching lower back, weak knees","zh":"腰痠膝軟"},"note":"<b>This is the answer.</b> Aching back and weak knees are the Kidney below — and their presence is what separates Liver Yang rising from plain Liver fire. He would never have volunteered it; you had to ask. 此即答案所在。腰痠膝軟為下焦腎虛，正是肝陽上亢與肝火上炎之分野。此症病人不會主動說，須問而後得。"},{"q":"How do you sleep, and how is your temper at home?","cq":"睡得如何？在家脾氣如何？","good":1,"a":"Badly. I wake at two and lie there furious about nothing.","ca":"睡不好。半夜兩點醒，躺著為些沒有的事生氣。","clue":{"en":"Insomnia and irritability","zh":"失眠、煩躁"},"note":"Yang that rises does not settle at night, and it disturbs the spirit. Irritability here is a symptom, not a character flaw — worth saying to the patient. 陽亢則夜不潛降，上擾心神。此煩躁是症，非其性，宜為病人言明。"},{"q":"Any trembling in the hands, slurred speech, or numbness down one side?","cq":"有沒有手抖、言語不清、或半身麻木？","good":1,"a":"No. Nothing like that, thank heaven.","ca":"沒有。謝天謝地，沒有那些。","clue":{"en":"No wind signs","zh":"無動風之象"},"note":"The exclusion that matters most. Rising yang can progress to <b>internal wind</b> — tremor, slurred speech, one-sided weakness, collapse. That picture is a stroke, and it leaves your room for urgent medical care immediately. 最要緊的排除。陽亢可進為肝風內動：震顫、言謇、半身不遂、猝倒——此即中風，當立即轉診急救，不可留治。"},{"q":"Is there a bitter taste, and are your stools dry?","cq":"口苦嗎？大便乾結嗎？","good":0,"a":"A little bitter in the mornings. Stools are ordinary.","ca":"早上有點苦。大便還算正常。","clue":"","note":"Reasonable — bitter taste is Gallbladder heat. But without red swollen eyes, constipation and a forceful rapid pulse, this stays short of Liver fire blazing upward. 問得合理，口苦屬膽熱。然無目赤腫、便秘、脈數有力，尚未至肝火上炎。"}],"look":[{"t":"Red body, thin yellow coating","c":"舌質紅，苔薄黃","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Red tongue, thin yellow coat","zh":"舌紅苔薄黃"},"note":"Correct. Red says heat; a thin coating says the heat has not congealed into a substantial pathogen. That fits yang that has risen rather than fire that has accumulated. 舌紅主熱；苔薄則熱未成形。合於陽亢而非火積。"},{"t":"Red body with a thick dry yellow coat","c":"舌紅，苔黃厚而燥","ok":0,"note":"That is Liver fire blazing upward — full heat with substance. It comes with red swollen eyes, constipation, and a wiry rapid forceful pulse. And crucially, <b>no</b> weak back and knees. 此為肝火上炎，實熱有形。當兼目赤腫、便秘、脈弦數有力，且無腰膝痠軟。"},{"t":"Pale body, thin white coat","c":"舌淡，苔薄白","ok":0,"note":"A pale tongue is emptiness without heat. His face flushes and his pulse is forceful — a pale tongue would contradict both. 舌淡為虛而無熱。其面赤脈勁，與舌淡不合。"},{"t":"Dark purple body with stasis spots","c":"舌紫暗有瘀斑","ok":0,"note":"Blood stasis. His pain is distending and moves with mood, not fixed and stabbing. 此為血瘀。其痛脹而隨情志，非固定刺痛。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Wiry and forceful 弦而有力","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Wiry forceful pulse","zh":"脈弦有力"},"note":"Correct. Wiry is the Liver; force means yang is genuinely full above. In a patient whose root is depleted you may also feel it thin at the deep level — wiry above, fine beneath. 弦者肝脈，有力則上部之陽確實。下元虧者，沉取或兼細——上弦下細，正合上實下虛。"},{"t":"Wiry and rapid, very forceful 弦數有力","ok":0,"note":"That degree of heat is Liver fire. Expect red swollen eyes, a bitter mouth throughout the day, constipation and a thick yellow coat. 此熱之甚者為肝火。當見目赤腫、終日口苦、便秘、苔黃厚。"},{"t":"Thready and weak 細弱","ok":0,"note":"Pure emptiness. He has a flushed face, loud tinnitus and a splitting head — there is something full here, whatever else is empty. 純虛之脈。其面赤、耳鳴聲大、頭痛劇，上部確有實象。"},{"t":"Soggy and moderate 濡緩","ok":0,"note":"Damp. No greasy coat, no heaviness, no loose stool. 主濕。本案苔不膩、身不重、便不溏。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — locate it. Which organ system?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：定位。病在何臟？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Liver and Gallbladder","c":"肝膽","ok":1,"note":"Temporal headache (Shaoyang), dizziness, tinnitus, flushed face, irritability, worse with anger, wiry pulse. Six findings, one organ. 顳痛屬少陽、眩暈、耳鳴、面赤、煩躁、遇怒而甚、脈弦。六症同歸一臟。"},{"t":"Heart","c":"心","ok":0,"note":"The Heart would lead with palpitations, chest oppression and a spirit that cannot settle. His insomnia is a consequence of yang rising, not the leading complaint. 心病當以心悸、胸悶、神不安為主。其失眠乃陽亢所擾，非主症。"},{"t":"Kidney alone","c":"單屬腎","ok":0,"note":"The Kidney is genuinely involved — but Kidney deficiency alone gives no flushed face, no loud tinnitus, no forceful pulse. It is half the picture, not the whole of it. 腎確有病，然單純腎虛不當見面赤、耳鳴聲大、脈有力。此為其半，非其全。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — above and below. Is this full, empty, or both?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：辨上下。實？虛？抑或上實下虛？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Full above and empty below — yang risen because the yin below no longer anchors it","c":"上實下虛 — 下不涵陽，陽升於上","ok":1,"note":"<b>This is the pattern, and this step is the whole chapter.</b> Above: headache, dizziness, tinnitus, flushed face, forceful pulse. Below: aching back, weak knees. The classic image is <b>water failing to moisten wood</b> — Kidney yin too depleted to hold the Liver's yang down. 此證之所在，亦本章之要義。上：頭痛、眩暈、耳鳴、面赤、脈有力。下：腰痠膝軟。所謂「水不涵木」，腎陰不足，不能潛肝陽。"},{"t":"Full throughout — Liver fire blazing upward","c":"純實 — 肝火上炎","ok":0,"note":"Fire is full heat with no deficiency underneath. The moment he told you his knees give way on the stairs, pure excess stopped being the answer. 肝火為純實熱，下無虛象。其言上樓腿軟，純實之說即不成立。"},{"t":"Empty throughout — Liver and Kidney yin deficiency","c":"純虛 — 肝腎陰虛","ok":0,"note":"Yin deficiency alone gives tidal fever, night sweats, five-centre heat and a thready rapid pulse — a quieter, drier picture. His pulse has force and his head is pounding. 純陰虛當見潮熱、盜汗、五心煩熱、脈細數，其象較靜而燥。本案脈勁頭脹，不然。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — branch and root. What do you treat first?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：標本先後。先治何者？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Both together — subdue the yang above while nourishing the yin below","c":"標本兼顧 — 平肝潛陽，兼滋肝腎之陰","ok":1,"note":"Correct. Treat only the branch and the headache returns the week you stop; treat only the root and he suffers for months while it slowly fills. When the branch is urgent but not dangerous and the root is clear, you work on both. 是。專治其標，停治即發；專治其本，緩不濟急。標急而未危、本明而可及者，當標本兼顧。"},{"t":"The root only — nourish Kidney yin and the yang will settle by itself","c":"專治其本 — 滋腎陰，陽自潛","ok":0,"note":"Eventually true, and too slow to be kind. He has had a splitting head for a year. Nourishing yin is slow work; give him some relief while it takes hold. 理雖不謬，而失之緩。其頭痛已一年。滋陰非旦夕之功，當先與之少安。"},{"t":"The branch only — subdue the yang, that is what he came for","c":"專治其標 — 潛其陽，此其所求","ok":0,"note":"That is treating the complaint instead of the patient. Suppress rising yang without refilling what should hold it down, and you have bought him a quiet fortnight. 此為治其所訴，非治其人。潛陽而不補其所以涵之者，不過得半月之安。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"GB20","t":"Fēngchí GB20 風池","ok":1,"note":"Subdues Liver yang and clears the head — the first point for dizziness, headache and rising yang. It works on both the exterior wind of an invasion and the interior wind of yang stirring. 平肝潛陽、清利頭目。眩暈、頭痛、陽亢之首選。外風內風皆可用之。"},{"id":"LR3","t":"Tàichōng LR3 太衝","ok":1,"note":"Source point of the Liver, and it draws downward. In rising yang its direction is the point: it pulls what has gone up back down. 肝之原穴，性主下行。陽亢者取其引上逆之氣下歸。"},{"id":"KI3","t":"Tàixī KI3 太谿","ok":1,"note":"Source point of the Kidney — the root of this pattern. Water that cannot moisten wood is Kidney yin too depleted to anchor the Liver. This is the point that refills it. 腎之原穴，本證之根。水不涵木者，腎陰不足以潛肝陽。補其陰，正在此穴。"},{"id":"LI4","t":"Hégǔ LI4 合谷","ok":0,"note":"With LR3 this is the Four Gates, and the Four Gates open <b>stagnation</b>. His qi is not stuck — it is rising. Opening the gates wider does not bring anything down. 與太衝合為四關，四關主開鬱。本案氣非鬱而是亢，開之無益於潛降。"},{"id":"ST36","t":"Zúsānlǐ ST36 足三里","ok":0,"note":"The instinct is right — there is emptiness to fill. But the emptiness is Kidney yin below, not Spleen qi in the middle. Tonifying the wrong axis in a patient with heat above can add to what is already rising. 補之之念不誤，然其虛在下焦腎陰，非中焦脾氣。上有熱而補其中，恐反助其升。"},{"id":"SP9","t":"Yīnlíngquán SP9 陰陵泉","ok":0,"note":"Drains damp. There is no damp — no greasy coat, no heaviness, no loose stool. 利濕之穴。本案無濕：苔不膩、身不重、便不溏。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Angle the needle toward the tip of the nose and control the depth — and use reducing above with reinforcing below","c":"針尖朝鼻尖，嚴控深度；上部用瀉，下部用補","ok":1,"note":"Correct on both counts. <b>GB20 sits below the occiput, near the foramen magnum.</b> Angling toward the nose tip or the opposite inner canthus, with controlled depth, keeps the needle away from the medulla — this is not a stylistic preference, and it is why GB20 gets so much attention in safe-needling training. And an upper-full lower-empty pattern is needled accordingly: drain what is excessive above, reinforce what is depleted below. 二者皆是。風池在枕骨下，近枕骨大孔。針尖向鼻尖或對側目內眥，嚴控深度，使不及延髓——此非手法偏好，故 CNT 於此穴著墨最多。又上實下虛者，上瀉下補，各如其分。"},{"t":"Needle straight in and deep, toward the opposite side, for a stronger effect","c":"直刺向對側深入，以求強效","ok":0,"note":"That is precisely the dangerous direction. Deep needling angled toward the midline at GB20 can reach the medulla. Never trade safety for sensation. 此正為危險方向。風池向內深刺可及延髓。不可以安全換針感。"},{"t":"Reducing method everywhere, since the yang is excessive","c":"通身皆用瀉法，陽亢故也","ok":0,"note":"Half right, and the half that is wrong costs you the case. Draining KI3 in a man whose Kidney yin is already short empties the very thing that must hold the yang down. 對了一半，錯的一半足以壞事。其腎陰本虧，復瀉太谿，是奪其所以潛陽者。"},{"t":"Moxa GB20 to warm and open the channel","c":"灸風池以溫通經絡","ok":0,"note":"Moxa warms. He has heat rising to his head, a red tongue and a flushed face. Adding warmth here works directly against the treatment principle. 灸主溫。其熱上衝、舌紅面赤，加溫適與治則相悖。"}]};
